    {
      "id": "UnXKFt4LxKjfSOH3Pr3NW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1280.5802307128906,
      "y": 342,
      "width": 667.8395385742188,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0m",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1654328468,
      "version": 860,
      "versionNonce": 525042220,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794495119781,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Every GPU has 2 speed limits:\noperations per second (cores) and bytes per second (global memory).\n\nCompute-bound: the cores are full. Memory keeps up easily.\n\nMemory-bound: the memory channels are full. Cores wait for data.\n\nMost kernels start out memory-bound. The cores calculate\nfaster than global memory can deliver.\n\nA kernel becomes compute-bound when it does many operations\nper byte fetched.\n\nRule of thumb: assume memory-bound until measured\notherwise.\n\nWhichever side is full sets the speed. The other side has\nroom to spare.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Every GPU has 2 speed limits:\noperations per second (cores) and bytes per second (global memory).\n\nCompute-bound: the cores are full. Memory keeps up easily.\n\nMemory-bound: the memory channels are full. Cores wait for data.\n\nMost kernels start out memory-bound. The cores calculate\nfaster than global memory can deliver.\n\nA kernel becomes compute-bound when it does many operations\nper byte fetched.\n\nRule of thumb: assume memory-bound until measured\notherwise.\n\nWhichever side is full sets the speed. The other side has\nroom to spare.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
